@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title OAuth login and the parallel session state:\nSharedServices authenticates the user at an identity provider, then maintains\nthe Session collection and the Registered Users collection side by side in MongoDB (Atlas)

actor "User" as User
participant "Browser / client" as Browser
participant "SharedServices\n(the Gate / UniversalNavigator)" as SS
participant "Identity provider\n(Google / Facebook / Apple OAuth)" as IdP

box "MongoDB (Atlas)" #f9fafb
  database "Registered Users\ncollection" as UsersCol
  database "Session\ncollection" as SessionCol
end box

== OAuth login ==

User -> Browser : choose "Log in with Google / Facebook / Apple"
Browser -> SS : GET /login?provider=<idp>
SS -> Browser : 302 redirect to the provider's authorize URL
Browser -> IdP : authorize (user authenticates and consents)
IdP -> Browser : redirect back to the callback with an authorization code
Browser -> SS : callback carrying the authorization code
SS -> IdP : exchange code for tokens + identity claims
IdP -> SS : id_token / userinfo (sub, email, name)

== the two collections are maintained in parallel ==

SS -> UsersCol : upsert user by provider sub (create on first login, else update)
UsersCol -> SS : user_id
SS -> SessionCol : insert session row {guid, token, signature, user_id}
SessionCol -> SS : ack
note over UsersCol, SessionCol
  Maintained in parallel: the Registered User (durable identity)
  and the Session (this visit) are separate collections, written
  side by side. A guest has a Session and no Registered User.
end note

note over SS
  token = "CH" + nonce(35) + guid(32)
  signature = RSA PKCS1v15 SHA256 over
  "origin:original_stamp:guid", signed with shared.key
end note

SS -> Browser : SessionToken{origin, token, signature,\ncreated_at, signed, server_env}

== later: every authenticated hop ==

Browser -> SS : call carries session_token\n(the Gate forwards it to the UniversalNavigator)
SS -> SS : SessionToken.verify(expected_origin)\nloads shared.crt, checks origin and length

alt signature verifies
  SS -> SessionCol : re-stamp nonce (put_nonce) and update the session row
  SessionCol -> SS : updated
  SS -> Browser : new token returned on the final event
else missing, malformed, or signature fails
  SS -> Browser : 401
end

note over SessionCol
  Nonce.restamp keeps the ORIGINAL stamp and replaces the
  LATEST one, so the token is re-signed over an unchanged
  payload. The GUID is stable for the whole session; the
  nonce changes on every receive. The session expires when
  expires_at has passed or the nonce is older than 300s.
end note

note over SS, IdP
  The UniversalNavigator is the only node that accepts external
  traffic; session verification, maintenance and timeouts are its
  helper functions. Cookies are not used: HuggingFace's edge proxy
  strips credentials from OPTIONS preflights, so the token rides in
  the body the gate forwards. Proxies carry tool-to-tool traffic
  only — no sessions.
end note

@enduml
